## Roster: Main Leaderboard vs Induction Queue

Two celebrity lists; **`tracked_people.status`** is the sole source of truth for which list someone is on:

- **`main_leaderboard`** — actively tracked (API ingest, `trending_people`, trend scores, native prediction markets, Weekly Jackpot eligibility).
- **`induction`** — shadow profile only (`tracked_people.status = 'induction'`). Not ingested or scored. Profile pages exist for comments/Voices; users vote via **`induction_candidates`** (`is_active = true`).

**Admin induction queue** (Celebrities filter and Voting CMS → Induction Queue): both surfaces show the same active candidates (`induction_candidates.is_active = true`), matched 1:1 by name to `tracked_people` shadow rows. Inactive/historical rows (promoted, rejected, archived) are admin history only — not a second queue.

**Historical trend snapshots:** induction people may have rows in `trend_snapshots` from a past accidental-tracking incident or from deliberate demotions from the main leaderboard. This is expected; all scoring/leaderboard/market queries gate on `status = 'main_leaderboard'` only.

---

## Prediction Markets

VoxDex offers five market types, all settled in virtual credits:

- **Up/Down** — Will [person]'s trend score go up or down by [date]? Binary outcome.
- **H2H (Head-to-Head)** — Which of two people will have the higher trend score by [date]? Binary outcome.
- **Top Gainer** (`marketType: gainer`) — Which person from a category will have the largest trend score increase over the market window? Multi-outcome.
- **Weekly Jackpot** (`marketType: jackpot`) — Weekly themed exact-score market with a pooled prize. **Stays parimutuel** (intentionally not migrated to AMM).
- **World Markets** (`marketType: community` in DB) — Real-world events (politics, sports, entertainment, etc.). Outcomes depend on external reality, not trend scores.

### World Market resolution is MANUAL — auto-resolve does not exist yet

Native markets (Up/Down, H2H, Gainer, Jackpot) settle automatically off trend snapshots via the 5-minute resolver cron. **World Markets do not.** A World Market past `endAt` moves to `CLOSED_PENDING` and waits for an admin to settle it in the AMM resolution dialog.

Three things propose but never settle — do not mistake any of them for automation:

- **Source watch** (`market-scout.ts`) — LLM-free Polymarket poll; pre-fills a proposed winner in `metadata.scoutAssessment` and can auto-lock trading (`AUTO_LOCK_ON_RESOLUTION_ENABLED`).
- **Resolution scout** (`resolution-scout.ts`, `RESOLUTION_SCOUT_LLM_ENABLED`) — daily GPT + web-search scan; advisory only, and always held by the auto-resolve gate (`llm_only_signal`).
- **`AUTO_RESOLVE_SHADOW_ENABLED`** — logs what auto-resolve *would* have done (`[AutoResolveShadow]`) next to what a human actually did (`[AutoResolveActual]`). **Zero side effects.** `AUTO_RESOLVE_MIN_CONFIDENCE` only tunes that log. Shipping real auto-resolve is a future task justified by this shadow data.

There is no production "un-resolve" endpoint: `resolveAmmMarket` is idempotent, so a wrong winner needs a targeted ops repair (see `ops/repair-knockout-draw-resolutions.ts`) or a void. Void refunds at net cost basis and is credit-safe.

### Scout drafts expire if not reviewed

`market-scout.ts` runs ~07:00 UTC and inserts World Markets as **`visibility: 'draft'`** — invisible to users *and* to agents, with no AMM seed until an admin publishes them. A draft whose `end_at` passes with no AMM state and no bets is auto-VOIDed and archived (`"Draft expired unpublished"`), so an unreviewed queue silently discards the scout's output. Zero agent activity on a World Market almost always means it is still a draft, not a liquidity bug.

### Market Engine: AMM/LMSR (native + World Markets only)

Up/Down, H2H, Top Gainer, and World Markets use **AMM with LMSR** pricing. Weekly Jackpot remains **parimutuel** — `generateWeeklyJackpot` sets `engine: 'parimutuel'` explicitly (`server/jobs/market-generator.ts`).

Native non-jackpot markets were migrated from parimutuel to AMM in a multi-phase rebuild (parimutuel resolver paths removed for new native markets; jackpot was always excluded).

- **Engine dispatch:** `prediction_markets.engine` is `'amm'` (default) or `'parimutuel'` (jackpot + legacy rows). Bet/settlement routes branch on engine. Cutoff helper: `getMarketBettingCutoff()` in `server/native-markets/lifecycle.ts`.
- **AMM state:** one `market_amm_state` row per AMM market (liquidity `b`, share quantities, house seed). Trades write a `market_bets` row with `action_type` = `buy` / `sell` (`parimutuel` for jackpot) and a matching `credit_ledger` entry whose `txn_type` is `amm_buy` / `amm_sell`. (Note: `amm_buy`/`amm_sell` are ledger txn types, not `market_bets.action_type` values.)
- **House singleton:** one `is_house` profile seeds AMM markets (`server/services/amm-house.ts`, fixed UUID in migrations).
- **AMM cutoff:** trading closes at `endAt − pre_resolve_cooldown` (default **5 minutes**, admin-tunable via `amm_runtime_settings`). Jackpot uses a separate weekly cutoff (Friday 23:59 UTC).
- **`buyCost` overflow guard:** `shared/lib/amm/lmsr.ts` switches formulas when `Δ/b` is large — preserve this.
- **Settlement is idempotent** — re-resolving an already-settled AMM market is a no-op (`server/services/amm-resolver.ts`).
- **Financial audit trail:** `credit_ledger` rows with idempotency keys; admin actions also log to `admin_audit_log`.

### Two-Path Agent System (market liquidity simulation)

~**56** V2 simulation agents (`server/agents/agentSeeder.ts`) place predictions to simulate human activity:

- **Native markets** (Up/Down, H2H, Top Gainer, Weekly Jackpot) — deterministic trait-vector engine using internal trend signals, with LLM-generated rationales/comments.
- **World Markets** (`community`) — GPT with web search via `worldMarketEngine.ts` when `WORLD_MARKETS_LLM_ENABLED=true` (budget-gated). Kill switch: set env to `false`.

Persona bands: sharp, casual, noisy, liquidity, whale. World-market bets are scheduled with staggered `executeAfter` delays to bootstrap liquidity before users arrive. Brier scores tracked on agent configs / admin tiles.

Key files: `agentRunner.ts` (orchestration), `decisionEngine.ts` (native picks), `worldMarketEngine.ts` (LLM + web search), `actionWorker.ts` (executes queued bets). Jackpot agents use exact-score `jackpot_bet`, not AMM shares.

**Rule:** Do not modify agent personas, dispatch logic, or settlement code without being explicitly asked. Phase 5 admin dashboard (`AdminAmmSection`) is for AMM ops/reconciliation only.

World Market LLM spend has **two** gates, and production currently runs with the second one off:

- `WORLD_MARKETS_LLM_ENABLED` — master switch for the world-market agent path (must be literal `true`/`1`/`yes`/`on` — Railway `TRUE` broke once).
- `WORLD_MARKETS_LLM_ASSESSMENTS_ENABLED` — **`false` in production.** With it off, agents bet on scouted markets using the zero-cost Polymarket `source_anchor` and simply abstain on unanchored/manual markets. `WORLD_MARKETS_DAILY_BUDGET_USD` is therefore largely inert today. Turning assessments back on will start real per-call spend against that budget — raise it first (the per-call reserve estimate is $0.40, so a $0.50 budget allows one call per day).

Flag-reading note: `envFlag` accepts `true`/`1`/`yes`/`on` case-insensitively, so Railway `TRUE` is safe now. For the convergence features, `*_SHADOW=true` **does not** mean "log only" when the matching `*_ENABLED` is also true — it adds extra logging on top of live behaviour. `MIDWEEK_CONVERGENCE`, `LATCH_REVERT`, and `COMMUNITY_CONVERGENCE` are all live in production despite their shadow flags being set.

